msgctxt "#30035"
msgid "Recordings"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30038"
msgid "Recordings/timers refresh interval (minutes)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30039"
msgid "How often to ask Kodi to re-check its recordings and timers list on its own, without waiting for a local action (like starting or deleting a recording from this Kodi) to prompt it. Without this, a change made another way -- from a different Kodi install sharing this Dispatcharr account, directly through Dispatcharr itself, or a recording finishing on its own with nothing local to react to it -- would only ever show up after restarting Kodi."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30040"
msgid "Enable real-time recording/timer updates (experimental)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30041"
msgid "Connects directly to Dispatcharr's own real-time update feed (the same one its own web interface uses -- no extra setup on the Dispatcharr side needed) so a change shows up in Kodi immediately instead of waiting for the refresh interval above. That interval keeps running as a fallback even with this on, in case the connection can't be made or drops and stays down. Experimental: this is new, hand-written networking code that hasn't seen the same real-world use as the rest of this addon -- leave off if you'd rather stick with the plain refresh interval."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30049"
msgid "Recurring timer: Dispatcharr's system timezone offset from UTC (minutes)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30050"
msgid "Only affects recurring (day-of-week) timers. Dispatcharr stores a recurring rule's start/end time-of-day as a plain wall-clock value with no timezone attached, and interprets it using its own configured system timezone (Settings -> System in Dispatcharr's web UI), not UTC -- this addon has no way to read that automatically and convert for you, since it doesn't bundle a full IANA timezone database. Set this to match Dispatcharr's configured system timezone's CURRENT offset from UTC, e.g. -360 for US Central Standard Time (UTC-6) or -300 for Central Daylight Time (UTC-5) -- if that zone observes daylight saving, you'll need to update this by 60 minutes twice a year yourself, or a recurring timer will fire an hour off until you do. Leave at 0 if Dispatcharr's system timezone is UTC. One-time and series timers are unaffected -- this only matters for the recurring timer type."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30047"
msgid "Improve catch-up seek reliability (experimental)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30048"
msgid "Routes catch-up/archive playback (play from guide) through the separate inputstream.ffmpegdirect addon (Kodi's official repository) instead of Kodi's own built-in seeking, which can be imprecise for raw MPEG-TS over HTTP. Experimental -- requires inputstream.ffmpegdirect to be installed, or catch-up playback will fail outright with this on. Leave off to use Kodi's default catch-up playback."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30030"
msgid "Advanced"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30031"
msgid "Enable verbose debug logging"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30032"
msgid "Logs full request/response details to the Kodi log. Leave off for normal use."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30033"
msgid "Dispatcharr API key"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30034"
msgid "Generated automatically on first connection and used only to play recordings, which Dispatcharr requires authentication for. Leave blank to have one generated for you -- only set this manually if you need to replace it (e.g. it was revoked or regenerated elsewhere), since regenerating one replaces the previous key for the whole account."
msgstr ""
